    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0639" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/661</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Greek Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Simopoulos</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-11">April 11, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I refer to your Note No. 995, dated March
                    29, 1934, in which you notified the Government of the United States that on
                    account of present difficulties the Greek Government is compelled to postpone,
                    in accordance with the option granted under Clause 2 of Part 1 of the debt
                    funding agreement of May 10, 1929, the payment of bond No. 13, dated January 1,
                    1928, maturing July 1, 1934, in the principal amount of $150,000.</p>
                <p>I am requested by the Secretary of the Treasury to advise you that the United
                    States takes notice of the action of your Government in this connection, and
                    also to advise you that, in accordance with the terms of the agreement, the
                    postponement is for a period of six months from July 1, 1934.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
